Fix mlx_lm qwen3_5 weight sanitization for VL checkpoints with tied embeddings.

Marlin-2B (model_type=qwen3_5, tie_word_embeddings=true) ships an explicit
`lm_head.weight` in its safetensors. mlx_lm's VL wrapper sanitize() prefixes
every un-prefixed checkpoint key with `language_model.`, so the key reaches
TextModel.sanitize() as `language_model.lm_head.weight` — but the tied-
embeddings drop only pops the un-prefixed name, and load_weights(strict=True)
then fails with:

    ValueError: Received 1 parameters not in model: language_model.lm_head.weight.

Apply to the installed mlx_lm (tested against mlx-lm 0.31.3 site-packages):

    cd <venv>/lib/python3.12/site-packages
    patch -p0 < mlx_lm_qwen3_5_tied_lm_head.patch

--- mlx_lm/models/qwen3_5.py
+++ mlx_lm/models/qwen3_5.py
@@ -314,6 +314,7 @@
         if self.args.tie_word_embeddings:
             weights.pop("lm_head.weight", None)
+            weights.pop("language_model.lm_head.weight", None)

         norm_keys = (
             ".input_layernorm.weight",
